WEBVTT

00:00:06.730 --> 00:00:07.860
Takahashi.

00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:13.820
I'll say this once, so listen carefully.

00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:21.120
I love you.

00:00:24.330 --> 00:00:25.330
No way...

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:37.800
Takahashi...

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:51.600
We kissed...

00:02:53.690 --> 00:02:57.690
It was with boy I've liked since spring...

00:02:57.690 --> 00:02:59.570
...and I had confessed to him once before, but...

00:03:00.570 --> 00:03:03.070
...I didn't really understand the response I got...

00:03:04.030 --> 00:03:06.490
...and I thought that it was all over for us.

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:11.080
Yet...

00:03:12.790 --> 00:03:14.080
I love you.

00:03:26.970 --> 00:03:29.350
As if it were a miracle...

00:03:29.350 --> 00:03:32.600
...I saw the entire world change before my eyes.

00:03:36.190 --> 00:03:38.610
Yano cast a spell on me.

00:03:43.910 --> 00:03:45.030
Morning!

00:03:45.030 --> 00:03:46.410
Good morning!

00:03:46.410 --> 00:03:47.700
Morning.

00:03:48.870 --> 00:03:51.410
I didn't get a wink of sleep.

00:03:53.210 --> 00:03:55.290
Morning.

00:03:55.290 --> 00:03:57.290
Nana, is your face puffy?

00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:01.590
What am I gonna do about my face?

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:04.550
Until yesterday...

00:04:06.010 --> 00:04:09.470
...he was a really annoying, loud-mouth classmate...

00:04:09.470 --> 00:04:12.430
...but because of what happened, I was up all night...

00:04:12.430 --> 00:04:14.270
...wondering how to face him today.

00:04:22.860 --> 00:04:23.950
Morning.

00:04:23.950 --> 00:04:25.910
G-Good morning.

00:04:32.910 --> 00:04:34.750
Hey, morning.

00:04:34.750 --> 00:04:36.540
That thing went pretty well the other day, don't you think?

00:04:38.340 --> 00:04:40.710
It's... it's no good...

00:04:43.050 --> 00:04:45.720
I might not be able to look him straight in the face anymore...

00:04:49.510 --> 00:04:50.970
Or so I thought...

00:04:50.970 --> 00:04:52.730
Hey, take a look at this. Looks cool, right?

00:04:52.730 --> 00:04:55.480
That's pretty awesome.

00:04:58.060 --> 00:04:59.440
Mizu-chin.

00:04:59.440 --> 00:05:01.980
You. Is it true that you and Yano kissed?

00:05:03.030 --> 00:05:04.900
What? When did...?!

00:05:04.900 --> 00:05:06.990
I won't forgive you! Spill the beans!

00:05:06.990 --> 00:05:09.620
No way... we were seen.

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:13.120
So, what's going on now? Are you two gonna go out?

00:05:13.700 --> 00:05:15.750
Huh? Oh, I see...

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:20.750
Sorry, but you'd better not come to me with your love problems anymore!

00:05:20.750 --> 00:05:24.380
Though I'll definitely support you when you're breaking up, so come to me for that!

00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:28.010
We'll be dating, won't we?

00:05:28.010 --> 00:05:30.350
Yano hasn't said anything to me yet...

00:05:31.140 --> 00:05:32.970
And I haven't gotten any text messages...

00:05:32.970 --> 00:05:35.980
But he never sent me any text messages before, either.

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:40.860
He's slowly starting to get on my nerves.

00:05:46.030 --> 00:05:47.030
Here he comes!

00:05:49.450 --> 00:05:50.320
Takahashi.

00:05:50.320 --> 00:05:51.870
Y-Y-Y-Yes?!

00:05:52.580 --> 00:05:54.870
Umm... they said that thing will be on Saturday.

00:05:56.080 --> 00:05:57.870
Ah... okay.

00:05:57.870 --> 00:05:59.000
I see...

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:02.340
You okay? You seem a little out of it today.

00:06:02.340 --> 00:06:04.340
I-It's because I couldn't get to sleep last night!

00:06:04.340 --> 00:06:05.760
Crap!

00:06:05.760 --> 00:06:07.380
Um, I mean...

00:06:07.380 --> 00:06:10.180
I'm such a moron for not being able to fall asleep over a kiss!

00:06:10.180 --> 00:06:13.470
And what was he talking about? He's reminding me about upcoming events?

00:06:13.470 --> 00:06:14.850
Repeat after me, then.

00:06:15.770 --> 00:06:17.180
Today, a student council meeting at three.

00:06:17.180 --> 00:06:19.140
Thursday, a student council event review meeting.

00:06:19.140 --> 00:06:20.520
Saturday, the event.

00:06:20.520 --> 00:06:22.480
Today, a student council meeting at three.

00:06:22.480 --> 00:06:23.070
Tuesday--

00:06:23.070 --> 00:06:23.730
Thursday.

00:06:23.730 --> 00:06:26.690
Thursday, the event review meeting.

00:06:26.690 --> 00:06:29.280
Today, a student council meeting at three. Lunch at twelve.

00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:30.410
Saturday, the event.

00:06:31.490 --> 00:06:34.280
Today, a student council meeting at three. Lunch at twelve.

00:06:34.280 --> 00:06:35.370
Thursday, the event.

00:06:35.370 --> 00:06:38.500
Moron. Saturday, the event. Today, a movie at four.

00:06:39.080 --> 00:06:40.710
Geez... what's up with him?

00:06:40.710 --> 00:06:41.710
Today, the student council meeting.

00:06:41.710 --> 00:06:42.960
Thursday, the event review meeting.

00:06:42.960 --> 00:06:43.960
Saturday, the event!

00:06:43.960 --> 00:06:45.090
Today, a movie at four!

00:06:45.090 --> 00:06:46.380
Correct! Good job.

00:06:49.470 --> 00:06:52.590
Today, a m-movie at four?

00:06:53.800 --> 00:06:57.060
A movie... at four?

00:06:58.810 --> 00:07:00.560
Ah, geez!

00:07:02.270 --> 00:07:05.020
My heart hasn't stopped pounding since this morning...

00:07:05.020 --> 00:07:07.440
...yet how can you say that stuff so easily?

00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:09.530
Don't give me that cute smile!

00:07:11.410 --> 00:07:14.950
Now that I feel so relieved, my sleepiness has caught up with me...

00:07:16.660 --> 00:07:20.290
Yano finally smiled at me today.

00:07:21.540 --> 00:07:23.420
It means it wasn't a fake.

00:07:23.420 --> 00:07:25.000
I wasn't taking it the wrong way.

00:07:26.340 --> 00:07:27.960
What happened yesterday really did...

00:07:34.430 --> 00:07:37.600
Geez, she's still sleeping!

00:07:37.600 --> 00:07:39.560
Didn't she sleep at all last night?

00:07:40.640 --> 00:07:43.560
Nana! The student council meeting's at three!

00:07:45.110 --> 00:07:48.400
A date... a date...

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:49.740
What am I gonna do...?

00:07:49.740 --> 00:07:51.200
I'm so nervous...

00:08:01.410 --> 00:08:04.210
Huh? It's already this late...

00:08:04.670 --> 00:08:07.130
Ah, the student council meeting...

00:08:07.130 --> 00:08:09.340
Shoot... it's long over...

00:08:13.720 --> 00:08:15.340
No way... no way!

00:08:15.340 --> 00:08:16.010
Ya--

00:08:22.390 --> 00:08:23.390
He lef--

00:08:25.980 --> 00:08:27.400
You're finally up.

00:08:31.860 --> 00:08:34.070
Y-You're still here?

00:08:34.070 --> 00:08:35.610
What do you mean?

00:08:36.240 --> 00:08:38.700
I went to the student council meeting in your place.

00:08:42.120 --> 00:08:43.460
I took notes for you, too.

00:08:44.160 --> 00:08:46.000
And here are the handouts.

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:49.460
You need to take survey during homeroom, and this is to be submitted next week.

00:08:52.010 --> 00:08:52.840
What?

00:08:53.800 --> 00:08:55.840
You went in my place?

00:08:55.840 --> 00:08:58.930
That's what I've been saying.

00:08:58.930 --> 00:09:01.810
I... I can't believe it...

00:09:01.810 --> 00:09:06.560
Yano, a guy who finds everything a pain and skips out all the time, did this?

00:09:14.700 --> 00:09:15.990
Can you make it to the movie?

00:09:25.290 --> 00:09:26.540
Ah, wait one sec.

00:09:28.130 --> 00:09:31.500
After watching the movie and getting something to drink, I wonder if we'll go out to eat, too...

00:09:31.500 --> 00:09:32.710
And I can't forget bus fare, either...

00:09:32.710 --> 00:09:34.800
Don't worry about that. I'll pay.

00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:36.180
I'll pay you back!

00:09:36.180 --> 00:09:38.010
I'll pay you back tomorrow, okay?

00:09:38.010 --> 00:09:38.840
You don't have to.

00:09:38.840 --> 00:09:40.140
No, I will.

00:09:48.350 --> 00:09:49.400
Here's an open seat.

00:09:50.270 --> 00:09:51.360
Go on, take it.

00:10:03.580 --> 00:10:05.330
Actually, I think I'll stand.

00:10:05.330 --> 00:10:07.160
It's gonna get more crowded, you know.

00:10:07.160 --> 00:10:08.370
I-It's okay.

00:10:11.960 --> 00:10:12.920
What?

00:10:12.920 --> 00:10:14.000
Nothing.

00:10:17.170 --> 00:10:19.550
I feel like I'm wearing myself out...

00:10:19.550 --> 00:10:21.300
I need to act natural... natural...

00:10:25.770 --> 00:10:26.810
What do you want to drink?

00:10:27.390 --> 00:10:30.310
U-Umm... h-hot chocolate.

00:10:30.980 --> 00:10:31.610
Here you go.

00:10:31.610 --> 00:10:32.820
Thanks.

00:10:32.820 --> 00:10:34.900
Looks like there are a lot of open seats.

00:10:34.900 --> 00:10:37.400
Ah! I should've asked for a milk tea....

00:10:38.530 --> 00:10:41.910
Ahh... I'm pushing myself too hard again... I need to act natural! Natural!

00:10:44.790 --> 00:10:48.000
I didn't know you liked movies, Yano.

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:49.160
Ah, yeah.

00:10:49.790 --> 00:10:51.630
Especially because it's so dark, if you know what I mean!

00:10:55.380 --> 00:10:56.800
You don't get it, do you?

00:11:00.380 --> 00:11:01.890
Mind if I rest my arm here?

00:11:01.890 --> 00:11:03.640
Ah, sure.

00:11:07.020 --> 00:11:10.060
Takahashi, you can also rest your arm here if you need to.

00:11:10.060 --> 00:11:11.230
Ah, yeah.

00:11:11.230 --> 00:11:12.150
Where...?

00:11:24.620 --> 00:11:26.910
The seat next to me...

00:11:28.040 --> 00:11:29.790
...is a lot closer than I thought.

00:11:34.960 --> 00:11:40.720
The movie was about a woman who kept passing by the one she loved without realizing it...

00:11:41.880 --> 00:11:43.220
Ah! There they go again!

00:11:44.090 --> 00:11:46.720
Hurry and let them meet each other!

00:11:48.600 --> 00:11:50.480
They were finally able to meet again...

00:12:04.370 --> 00:12:05.820
Finger exercises.

00:12:21.420 --> 00:12:23.800
No... it's nothing.

00:12:25.510 --> 00:12:29.770
He... kept half of the armrest free the entire time...

00:12:48.080 --> 00:12:50.040
And that's when I thought...

00:12:51.500 --> 00:12:53.790
...that having mutual feelings for each other is great.

00:13:01.960 --> 00:13:02.630
Mizu-chin's...

00:13:02.630 --> 00:13:03.510
...and Taka-chan's...

00:13:03.510 --> 00:13:05.090
"We Were There Too!"

00:13:05.090 --> 00:13:06.430
Hi there! I'm Mizuguchi!

00:13:06.430 --> 00:13:07.340
And I'm Nagami!

00:13:07.340 --> 00:13:08.640
Moving straight to our topic of the day...

00:13:08.640 --> 00:13:09.100
Yes, yes?

00:13:09.100 --> 00:13:10.760
What's up with Nanami kissing him?!

00:13:10.760 --> 00:13:12.140
Yeah, I was really surprised!

00:13:12.140 --> 00:13:13.020
It makes me want to cry!

00:13:13.020 --> 00:13:16.600
In the first place, when... when did Nanami fall for Yano, anyway?!

00:13:16.600 --> 00:13:18.110
Now, now, calm down, Mizu-chin.

00:13:18.110 --> 00:13:21.820
I'll never listen to her love problems ever again!

00:13:21.820 --> 00:13:24.450
But we can't just leave Nanami alone, can we?

00:13:24.450 --> 00:13:25.070
But...!

00:13:25.070 --> 00:13:25.950
But I can't forgive her!

00:13:25.950 --> 00:13:27.450
And so...

00:13:27.450 --> 00:13:29.990
Please enjoy the second half of the show!

00:13:31.240 --> 00:13:32.950
That movie was really good, huh?

00:13:32.950 --> 00:13:33.700
You think so?

00:13:33.700 --> 00:13:35.910
Yeah! The ending was really moving!

00:13:35.910 --> 00:13:38.000
What scenes did you like, Yano?

00:13:38.000 --> 00:13:38.960
Me?

00:13:38.960 --> 00:13:40.130
I...

00:13:41.050 --> 00:13:42.380
...liked the part where we held hands.

00:13:44.260 --> 00:13:49.930
I wonder if it's because I got so whirled up today...

00:13:49.930 --> 00:13:52.390
Yano just seems different than normal.

00:13:53.100 --> 00:13:57.230
They way he speaks, and his behavior... The intonation in his voice.

00:13:57.230 --> 00:13:59.190
They're all different than normal.

00:14:00.770 --> 00:14:01.650
Are you sleepy?

00:14:02.730 --> 00:14:04.150
Not at all.

00:14:04.150 --> 00:14:07.530
I'd feel bad if I made you go out of your way today.

00:14:07.530 --> 00:14:09.070
Let's go home after we finish eating.

00:14:12.370 --> 00:14:13.200
Yano.

00:14:13.200 --> 00:14:15.080
Why are you being so kind?

00:14:15.080 --> 00:14:17.580
What do you mean?

00:14:18.170 --> 00:14:19.250
Why?

00:14:19.250 --> 00:14:21.340
I'm a kind person, under everything.

00:14:21.340 --> 00:14:22.800
T-That's not what I meant.

00:14:23.460 --> 00:14:25.210
It's just so strange.

00:14:25.210 --> 00:14:28.300
Up until the other day, you were mean to me all the time...

00:14:28.880 --> 00:14:32.050
So why did you suddenly become such different person?

00:14:32.050 --> 00:14:36.060
Before you told me you loved me, did you not love me?

00:14:37.060 --> 00:14:39.980
You're the one who's changed.

00:14:41.230 --> 00:14:44.400
Obviously, my girlfriend isn't the same as my other classmates.

00:14:44.400 --> 00:14:47.440
To me, you're the one who's become different from before.

00:14:48.900 --> 00:14:50.990
T-That's...

00:14:50.990 --> 00:14:53.490
His girlfriend...

00:14:53.490 --> 00:14:54.620
What does he mean?

00:14:56.370 --> 00:14:58.000
His girlfriend...

00:14:58.000 --> 00:15:02.210
This basically means that you're an insider in my circle.

00:15:04.000 --> 00:15:05.420
An insider?

00:15:05.420 --> 00:15:11.680
Yeah. Everyone else is split into insiders and outsiders, right?

00:15:11.680 --> 00:15:13.220
What do you mean? That's weird.

00:15:17.350 --> 00:15:18.480
Is it really that strange?

00:15:19.850 --> 00:15:21.190
What am I gonna do...?

00:15:23.110 --> 00:15:24.320
Right now, I...

00:15:24.320 --> 00:15:27.900
...really want to hold Yano tightly.

00:15:38.000 --> 00:15:41.000
I've never been with anyone special for this event before...

00:15:41.000 --> 00:15:43.210
...but this year, it's different!

00:15:43.210 --> 00:15:46.920
But the problem here is that Yano has a better sense for this sort of stuff than me...

00:15:46.920 --> 00:15:50.380
I have to be careful so he doesn't say something like "laaame" to what I get him.

00:15:50.380 --> 00:15:51.510
This'll be tough...

00:15:52.260 --> 00:15:55.140
I wonder what sort of things make boys happy?

00:15:58.310 --> 00:15:59.310
W-What?

00:16:00.520 --> 00:16:01.730
Nothing.

00:16:03.560 --> 00:16:07.730
Even though he doesn't have anything to say, Yano unexpectedly comes really close sometimes.

00:16:07.730 --> 00:16:10.440
But only when no one's around.

00:16:10.440 --> 00:16:12.490
He's just like a cat.

00:16:12.490 --> 00:16:13.910
Ah, Yano.

00:16:13.910 --> 00:16:17.240
Is there anything you want for Christmas?

00:16:17.240 --> 00:16:18.080
Nana-chan!

00:16:20.910 --> 00:16:23.040
I'd like you to answer seriously.

00:16:27.460 --> 00:16:28.380
Worcester sauce!

00:16:28.380 --> 00:16:29.590
Oh, it's Yano.

00:16:30.170 --> 00:16:30.880
No, it's definitely Worcester sauce!

00:16:30.880 --> 00:16:31.920
And just when I thought they weren't getting along.

00:16:31.920 --> 00:16:33.130
It's definitely soy sauce!

00:16:33.130 --> 00:16:33.800
Worcester sauce!

00:16:33.800 --> 00:16:34.840
Soy sauce!

00:16:34.840 --> 00:16:35.720
Worcester sauce!

00:16:35.720 --> 00:16:37.550
I keep telling you, it's all about the soy sauce!

00:16:37.550 --> 00:16:39.560
Ah, Takeuchi-kun.

00:16:39.560 --> 00:16:40.560
Hey.

00:16:42.310 --> 00:16:43.600
Long time no see.

00:16:43.600 --> 00:16:44.520
I'm going to the bathroom.

00:16:46.270 --> 00:16:47.940
What were you two arguing about?

00:16:47.940 --> 00:16:51.490
Huh? Oh, which is better on sunny-side up eggs, soy sauce or Worcester sauce.

00:16:52.860 --> 00:16:54.780
We must seem like stupid love birds...

00:16:54.780 --> 00:16:55.570
Not at all.

00:16:56.740 --> 00:16:57.780
I'm glad, though.

00:17:00.040 --> 00:17:01.540
It's soy sauce!

00:17:02.410 --> 00:17:05.250
No matter what anyone says, soy sauce will remain on top!

00:17:05.250 --> 00:17:06.540
He sure shows off...

00:17:08.420 --> 00:17:10.590
It's deja vu...

00:17:13.380 --> 00:17:16.800
Geez... I didn't think you could be such a doofus.

00:17:17.890 --> 00:17:19.510
You're unexpectedly childish, aren't you?

00:17:20.470 --> 00:17:22.180
Let's go get some pizza.

00:17:22.180 --> 00:17:24.850
Geez, how do you have so much money?

00:17:24.850 --> 00:17:26.850
You don't even have a part-time job.

00:17:27.150 --> 00:17:28.860
My parents give me whatever I ask for.

00:17:29.860 --> 00:17:31.440
That must be nice.

00:17:31.440 --> 00:17:34.860
My parents are really stingy, and they won't even give me allowance.

00:17:35.990 --> 00:17:38.490
I bum money off them by doing the whole filial piety thing.

00:17:45.120 --> 00:17:46.330
Let's hold hands.

00:17:50.540 --> 00:17:53.840
Yano's hand is warm.

00:17:55.380 --> 00:18:00.680
That's why... whenever I touch it, my heart lets out a small squeal of joy.

00:18:03.930 --> 00:18:05.600
Why's your hand so cold?

00:18:06.480 --> 00:18:08.850
Girls are more sensitive to the cold.

00:18:11.190 --> 00:18:14.740
Yano, what do you want for your present?

00:18:14.740 --> 00:18:17.660
Ah, and this time, excluding living things.

00:18:21.950 --> 00:18:23.580
I don't really need anything.

00:18:23.580 --> 00:18:24.700
Don't say that.

00:18:26.000 --> 00:18:31.960
Yano must've realized that I only have a small allowance...

00:18:31.960 --> 00:18:34.550
He's really watching out for me...

00:18:34.550 --> 00:18:37.970
But... I want to give him something.

00:18:39.840 --> 00:18:41.470
Just as long as you're there, Takahashi.

00:18:42.970 --> 00:18:44.390
Ah, gross!

00:18:44.390 --> 00:18:45.810
W-What?

00:18:45.810 --> 00:18:48.060
Sorry. It was just so embarrassing to say.

00:18:48.060 --> 00:18:50.850
Ah... there's such bad taste in my mouth now!

00:18:50.850 --> 00:18:52.310
Yeah, yeah...

00:18:53.730 --> 00:18:55.320
Moron...

00:19:14.800 --> 00:19:16.840
Winter came quickly this year.

00:19:23.970 --> 00:19:27.560
But my heart is warm and cozy!

00:19:27.560 --> 00:19:28.850
Just kidding.

00:19:29.230 --> 00:19:31.980
And I kinda feel like I've become prettier!

00:19:31.980 --> 00:19:33.400
Could it be because of love?

00:19:33.400 --> 00:19:36.230
You serious? Talk about bad taste in girls!

00:19:37.990 --> 00:19:38.940
So ugly.

00:19:38.940 --> 00:19:40.070
She's so ugly, so why did he...?

00:19:40.070 --> 00:19:41.490
It's so annoying.

00:19:43.120 --> 00:19:45.620
Really... young girls these days.

00:19:46.490 --> 00:19:48.910
They're just jealous, so don't take it to heart.

00:19:50.290 --> 00:19:53.130
What?! They were talking about me? "Ugly" and all?

00:19:54.250 --> 00:19:57.800
I guess I'm now in a position where people are jealous of me...

00:20:00.550 --> 00:20:01.510
I'm sure...

00:20:08.560 --> 00:20:10.980
...there are a lot of other girls who cried, too.

00:20:14.310 --> 00:20:17.900
So, what do you want for your Christmas present?

00:20:17.900 --> 00:20:18.980
I don't need anything.

00:20:21.070 --> 00:20:23.530
Yano likes the snow.

00:20:24.700 --> 00:20:27.490
Hey, am I ugly?

00:20:30.580 --> 00:20:35.250
Ugly girls are more... impressive with their looks, to put it a certain way.

00:20:36.710 --> 00:20:38.250
Then, am I beautiful?

00:20:39.050 --> 00:20:41.220
Beautiful girls are more...

00:20:41.220 --> 00:20:42.930
Never mind.

00:20:42.930 --> 00:20:44.260
Honest bastard.

00:20:46.010 --> 00:20:49.520
What did you find attractive about me, Yano?

00:20:51.350 --> 00:20:53.520
You're cute, Takahashi.

00:20:55.270 --> 00:20:59.230
Why do I sometimes get anxious like this?

00:20:59.230 --> 00:21:00.320
Takahashi.

00:21:00.320 --> 00:21:01.740
Let me borrow your hands.

00:21:19.090 --> 00:21:24.470
When Yano touches me with his warm hands, my heart clenches up...

00:21:24.470 --> 00:21:27.430
I've decided on what I want for a Christmas present.

00:21:28.850 --> 00:21:30.430
Give me a promise.

00:21:32.220 --> 00:21:34.690
Promise me that you'll never leave my side.

00:21:42.110 --> 00:21:43.280
That you'll never...

00:21:44.860 --> 00:21:48.820
That you'll never ever betray me.

00:21:53.000 --> 00:21:54.710
Speaking honestly for a second...

00:21:55.330 --> 00:21:56.710
I don't know.

00:21:59.130 --> 00:22:02.460
I thought I'd never be able to go out with anyone again.

00:22:04.720 --> 00:22:07.180
Do you really, really like someone like me?

00:22:08.300 --> 00:22:09.300
Is it funny?

00:22:12.310 --> 00:22:13.680
Over something small like that...

00:22:15.270 --> 00:22:16.690
"Something small like that..."

00:22:19.560 --> 00:22:21.400
She...

00:22:21.400 --> 00:22:24.190
...died together with the guy she loved.

00:22:25.320 --> 00:22:29.200
I won't ever feel sympathy for her.

00:22:43.590 --> 00:22:45.510
It's as if...

00:22:45.510 --> 00:22:46.630
...the puzzle...

00:22:48.630 --> 00:22:51.010
...was slowly falling into place...

00:22:51.010 --> 00:22:52.550
...piece by piece.

00:23:12.410 --> 00:23:13.990
Someone beloved to me...

00:23:17.330 --> 00:23:21.830
I first learned what that meant... during the winter when I was fifteen years old.
